                <pb facs="0493" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg483"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–107</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">international
                            commission<lb/>at teschen</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-12-03"
                            >3 <hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi>, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Note to the Supreme
                    Council</hi>]</p>
                <p>The International Commission at Teschen, on account of the short duration of its
                    mandate, should assume no part of the administration of the country;
                    consequently, it shall have no local revenue to collect, and the totality of its
                    expenses shall be advanced by the Allied Governments.</p>
                <p>It seems advisable that each Power advance the amount of the expenses for its
                    Delegation. As to the common expenses of the entire Commission (Secretariat,
                    interpreters, rents, heating, light, etc,) they may be either advanced by that
                    of the Powers to which the President belongs, or covered by equal advances made
                    by the various Powers, represented in the Commission. A decision should be taken
                    to that effect.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
